- `constructor-unit-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests`

**How to implement.** Red first: an analytic model lowers to DATA, so equal models lower to equal axes (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.1). Facts only. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` add `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`. It uses the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator coefficient sets of `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:306-326`). For each model, lowering it twice through `toEpsAxis`, and lowering two separately built equal models, MUST give equal `EpsAxisDispersion` values with equal hashes, and `toEpsValue` MUST give equal `EpsWithDispValue` values. A model whose `bandGap` (Tauc-Lorentz) or `energy` (Gaussian) differs MUST lower to an unequal axis. The fact is red on the start tree: both models lower to `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:766-769`), a fresh closure on every call, which the custom equality compares by reference (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:386`).

**Acceptance.** After the fact lands, constructor-unit-tests (DispersionModelsTests) MUST fail with exactly `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`, failing on the first equality of two lowered axes; every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
